Kikyo-san's note ends here.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Checking the original, it seems to end here too.<PG>
It connects after all.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Is <STYLE ID="1">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE>, then, the main body of the fungus disguised as a cherry tree?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If so, then this ecology, far too abnormal to be called a cherry, makes a certain amount of sense.<PG>
Corpses walking around, a green-eyed sacrifice to defeat <STYLE ID="1">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE>...
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I can't tell whether it's a metaphor, but it's all vague and doesn't sit right.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Well, for now, taking in the information comes before working it out.<PG>
A fungus that disguises itself as the cherry and <STYLE ID="13" RUBY="つ">possesses</STYLE> people, known as <STYLE ID="1">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE>.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
What seems to contain all of it is this last book―
{PAUSE ""}
'The Ecology of <STYLE ID="1">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE>'
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
All of it is written in Japanese close to the modern language.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
