{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">However, our continued research into Droga has raised the possibility that the Arata cherry itself, the raw material of Droga, is an entity that brings disaster upon human beings.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">As the earlier research has also made clear, Droga extends its reach through infection by blood.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">What had long been the problem was the life cycle of the Arata cherry―</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="3">that is, how it grows and how it reproduces.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Since it has the property of using human beings as a medium, the possibility that it is a threat to humans from a biological standpoint cannot be ruled out. We have therefore continued our research into Droga and the Arata cherry.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">However, the fruiting bodies brought from the Arata settlement had almost entirely perished, and we had only about 100 ampules of Droga, so planned experiments were necessary.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n0\r\n3000\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\サード\世代説明.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
<EVENT VALUE="STOPMOVIE">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">What was needed first was confirmation of the fourth generation.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The existence of every generation up to the third had been confirmed, but the third generation almost all died in a frenzy or were caught up in killings among the test subjects.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">However, since a researcher who tried to stop the killing at the time was splashed with their blood and showed no change whatever, we concluded that no fourth generation arises by the same route of infection.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Yet in that case the reproduction of the Arata cherry would come to a halt, and so a hypothesis was formed that the fourth generation might arise by some other route.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That is, infection not by third-generation blood but by some other means.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">What drew attention here was the presence of the spores found in the first and second generations.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Since Arata cherries as small as fine particles have germinated inside their bodies, the hypothesis was put forward that by some means these sprouts could be made into cherry trees.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">If that hypothesis is correct, the infected other than the third generation become seedbeds for fruiting bodies, and extremely efficient reproduction of fruiting bodies becomes possible.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\荒田集落イメージ.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">We went to the Arata settlement, consulted the old documents, and formed a further hypothesis.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">In the past, an incident called 'the Green-Eye Curse-Killing' occurred, and on two occasions residents vanished and ended as cherry trees.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Might it not be, then, that the Green-Eye Curse-Killing acts as some kind of trigger?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">In that case, what can be called the trigger from a scientific standpoint is 'the presence of the corpse of a third-generation person who died at the end of the urge to kill.'</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{DELETECG "000" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">In our research up to now, too, there were corpses of third-generation subjects seized by the urge to kill, but they were promptly cremated.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">What, then, if the first and second generations had the opportunity to touch such a corpse for a long time?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">At a certain point, the Church's upper ranks arranged personnel usable as third generation for the experiment.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Whether it is true is unknown, but there was talk of a plea bargain with a condemned prisoner.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\エデン\赤い細胞イメージ.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">Two other test subjects were also provided; one was given Droga, and the others were made to touch the blood in turn, becoming second and third generation.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">First Generation (I)</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Second Generation (II)</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Third Generation (III)</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">―so we name them.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">When (II) and (III) were made to inhale cherry pollen, the familiar precognition appeared in (II), and (III) went mad.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Having confirmed that (III) was seized by the urge to kill (II), we had no choice but to shoot it dead.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Afterward, (I) and (II) were housed together with Corpse (III).</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">As a result, changes were observed in (I) and (II).</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">One week into cohabitation―</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="3">Once the decay of (III) had advanced somewhat, (I) and (II) (hereafter 'the mutated') began to show </STYLE><STYLE ID="6" RUBY="こうこつ">rapt</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> expressions and increasing delusional talk.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">When we listened to the mutated, they said:</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">'Soon we return to the earth.'</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">'Corpse (III) is waiting.'</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">―so they declared.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Even with cherry pollen withheld, the symptoms did not change, and they progressed regardless of the season.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\エデン\解剖セット.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">Meanwhile, when Corpse (III) was autopsied, extremely fine sprouts were confirmed to have formed on the skin.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">These, too, were extremely small, but there were spores at the tips of the sprouts.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">However, since the spores that formed on the corpse were sexual spores, they cannot germinate on their own.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That is, other spores that combine with the sexual spores formed on the corpse are required.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">When the blood of the mutated was sampled, the 10-micron sprouts had grown to about 100 microns, and at their tips sexual spores different from those of Corpse (III) were confirmed.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Most of those spores had already conjugated with the corpse's spores, and here, for the first time, we were able to confirm the existence of the fourth generation.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The fourth generation is the life form that results when the first and second generations undergo further mutation.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYMOVIE "桜散る.wmv" "256" "C" "C" "REPEAT" "FALSE" "0" "0"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n255\r\n3000\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{DELETECG "000" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n255\r\n0\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">A year later, the two mutants died in spring, and from the left chest a cherry tree about 3 meters tall emerged (there was a ceiling, so growth is thought to have stopped at 3 meters).</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It had already flowered, and outwardly it closely resembled the Somei-yoshino cherry.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That cherry used not soil but the two mutants as its seedbed, and a week later both trees had withered and died.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">As with ordinary fungi, unless the mutants die on organic matter such as soil, the fruiting bodies presumably cannot grow stably.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The site had a concrete floor, so it is thought they could not take root.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">When they were found, most of the corpses' muscle, skin and internal organs had dissolved, and a colorless, transparent mucus had spread across the floor.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">As in the earlier research, this is thought to be the effect of the petal-shaped digestive vacuoles, which occurred in order to use the seedbed corpses as a source of nutrients.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The traits of the fourth generation are summarized as follows.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">・It forms when the spores in the bodies of the first and second generation combine with the spores that form on a third-generation corpse</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">・The spores conjugate inside the bodies of the first and second generation (the first and second generation transition into the fourth generation)</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">・</STYLE><STYLE ID="6" RUBY="こうこつ">Rapt</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> expressions and delusional talk are observed</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">・The symptoms progress gradually, with a tendency to dote on Corpse (III)</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">・A year after spore conjugation, a cherry tree grows from the first- or second-generation person, who dies</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">The Arata cherry stores in its roots spores that produce a body-strengthening component, has mammals ingest them, and germinates inside the mammal's body.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">These lie hidden in the body until the grandchildren's generation, in which they make the hosts kill one another and release sexual spores.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The first and second generation who absorb them become fruiting bodies, and the range of reproduction spreads.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">This is the life cycle of the Arata cherry.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">As stated in the earlier research as well, the Arata cherry is a fungus, and a single organism.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The reason it parasitizes mammals in this way to multiply its fruiting bodies is thought to be that the hosts' mobility makes it easier to extend its range of growth.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">And its mimicry of the cherry is presumably meant to be the first to draw insects in early spring, when there are still few flowers.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Where insects come, small animals come. Where small animals come, larger animals come too.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">In this way, a small food chain arises around the fruiting bodies.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">In the past, this fungus seems to have been called </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">And in the Arata settlement, a third-generation girl preserved as a mummy is said to lie sleeping.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Should this come to light, anyone who has ever used Droga would at once be enthralled by the mummy, and a year later would die as a cherry tree.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">However, there is still something we do not understand.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It concerns 'the </STYLE><STYLE ID="15" RUBY="たけ">Fierce</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> Sound.'</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It is possible that the pulsing of the giant body of </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> underground opens small, deep fissures in the earth, and that air passing through them sounds like a brass instrument.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Furthermore, though this is a conjecture of ours―</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
{MESOFF "500"}
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n0\r\n3000\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "3000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<EVENT VALUE="STOPMOVIE">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> appears to have the ability to move corpses.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "エデンの桜\Brutal.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\エデン\死体目.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "20" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "2000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">When the aforementioned mutants (fourth generation) were dissected, hyphae had already spread throughout the brain, and its function as a brain had ceased completely.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Nevertheless, until the day before the trees grew, they had continued to act like living human beings.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">From the dissection, it is surmised that the brains were invaded by hyphae at least a month before death.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">For a month, they moved about while dead.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">The old documents contain an account that those infected with Droga who heard 'the Fierce Sound' vanished and became cherry trees, but this is thought to be mistaken.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">For when we conducted the experiment to create the fourth generation, no such sound was needed.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The reason for becoming fourth generation is the sexual union of the spores released from a third-generation corpse with the spores remaining in the bodies of the first and second generation.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">At the time the old documents were written, people went missing just as 'the Fierce Sound' rang out, so the writers presumably linked the two without scientific grounds.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Still, it is unlikely, at the least, that corpses and 'the Fierce Sound' have nothing to do with each other.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">The Shiyo 482 document, too, records that corpses overran the land and giant cherry trees grew.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The descriptions in this part are vague on many points and nothing definite can be said, but 'corpses overrunning the land' also ties in with the experimental results above.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">As for the giant cherry trees, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">, with its extremely large mycelial mat, may well be able to grow fruiting bodies larger than usual.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Yes―everything up to this point is exactly as recorded in 'The Teachings of Cerejeira,' left by the saint who is the ancestor of us of the Holy Cerejeira Church, Lord Ginosuke Niimura.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That is no scripture.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It is scientific data, a record of observations in the field.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">To return to the subject, the mechanism by which </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> controls corpses is unknown.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">But why does </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> need such an ability?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That too is probably a question bound up with the life cycle of </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">But for experiments in moving corpses, our knowledge, our facilities and the times themselves have not yet caught up.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">This study ends here, but the whole of the ecology of </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> has not been revealed.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Something important still remains.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Let us say beforehand that from here on, more conjecture is mixed in.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Yet because it is important, we ask that whoever has been granted the authority to see this understand that fully.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">If 'the </STYLE><STYLE ID="15" RUBY="たけ">Fierce</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> Sound' is in truth the movement of </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> underground, it must be making quite large motions, not merely extending hyphae.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Though it is a fungus, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> is able to move.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It is presumably a slow, limited movement, on the order of a carnivorous plant's, but why does it move?</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">If the third generation were to die out at the end of their killing one another, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> would lose its chance to grow.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">For a living thing, culling the infected is a contradiction.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">What we focused on, given that contradiction and the 'movement,' is the Arata settlement's custom of burial in the earth.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">The idea is this: if it can move corpses, might it not preserve them by some means?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It preserves the buried corpses of the Droga-infected until the proper time, and revives them when fruiting bodies are needed.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">However, wild dogs and other animals with a keen nose may dig up even buried corpses and eat them.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It is therefore necessary to move the corpses to a depth from which they cannot ordinarily be dug up.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">At such times, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> must make quite a large movement.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">By methods such as chemical preservation or freezing, it is possible to keep a dead body artificially for a long time.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Likewise, if </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> has an enzyme that can preserve corpses, then 800 years' worth of corpses lie sleeping intact beneath the Arata settlement.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">In this way, when fruiting bodies are needed, it uses the bodies of the Droga-infected to grow cherry trees.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">However, this alone is thin grounds for the claim that </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> moves and preserves corpses.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">One more reason for this conjecture is that cherry trees grow evenly throughout the Arata district.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">The Arata settlement has a graveyard clearing, and the dead are buried there.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That being so, many cherry trees ought to grow in the graveyard clearing. Yet only short grass grows there, and not a single tree, let alone a cherry.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">If cherry trees grew only in the graveyard clearing, the Arata cherry's range of reproduction would be severely limited.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Of course, it is quite possible that it uses mammals other than humans as seedbeds, but that would explain its growing evenly throughout the Arata district, not why no cherry trees grow in the graveyard clearing.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That is, it is surmised that </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> moves the corpses buried in the graveyard clearing and replants them in places suited to extending its range of reproduction.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">These are the grounds for 'the Fierce Sound' ringing out.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Underground, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> stirs, preserves corpses below the ground, and makes them seedbeds for cherry trees in suitable places.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Shifts in the ground therefore occur below, and fissures may open at the surface.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">'The Fierce Sound,' then, can be said to ring out when </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> displays some kind of activity.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">When that happens, what we must be most wary of is the presence of 'intelligence.'</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">The second and third generations possess precognition.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Why does </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> bring about such a mutation in the infected?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That is, it does not grant precognition; it shows visions and voices that look like precognition.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Looked at the other way, that is something it cannot do unless </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">, for its part, grasps the situation of the infected.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">What may be considered its most terrifying trait is the theft of the senses.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Since no apt phrase comes to hand, here we name it '</STYLE><STYLE ID="16" RUBY="とうかん">sense-theft</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">.'</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Sense-theft is </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> perceiving the sight and hearing of those who have precognition.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">It is a rather far-fetched idea, but otherwise there is no explaining precognition.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Since precognition is limited to 'danger sense,' those around a precognitive will readily take what the precognitive says </STYLE><STYLE ID="17" RUBY="うの">at face value</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">That way, to some degree, the society of living things can be manipulated as </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> wishes.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">But fungi have no brains to begin with, and cannot think or make judgments.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">This is where, at last, the control of corpses </STYLE><STYLE ID="18" RUBY="つな">ties in</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">When someone recently dead is buried, the </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> in the earth extends hyphae into the body and preserves it whole.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Then, by planting spores or hyphae in the brain, a faithful servant is born.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">These commandeered bodies, we surmise, are what </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3">'s intelligence is </STYLE><STYLE ID="19" RUBY="いしずえ">founded</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> on, and the large 'movement' is what is needed to hide the bodies.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">In other words, by using the brains of the dead, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> gains the ability to think.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\エデン\蔵本乱雑.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3">These are no more than conjectures.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">No, we know that this is too great a stretch.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">But when we try to make sense of its ecology, it inevitably comes out this way.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">At present there is only one way to test whether this account of its ecology is correct.</STYLE><PG>
{STOPSND "BGM" "0" "PASS"}
<STYLE ID="3">Have someone who has gained precognition through Droga read this report.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">And do so inside the Arata settlement, with their safety fully secured.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">Most likely, </STYLE><STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> will sense-steal it and regard the reader as a danger.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="8">Shigatsu Youka</STYLE><STYLE ID="3"> has hidden its own existence until now, so this report should be a threat to it.</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="3">If you who are reading this have precognition.</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="3">If our surmise is correct, then after this,</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "環境音\アポカリプティック2.ogg" "SE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{DELETECG "000" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="3"><TXSPS>'the Fierce Sound' will ring out, controlled corpses will appear, </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="3">and they will kill you―</STYLE>
{WAIT "100" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "文字カウント画像" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
<PG>
{}
